#### 07: the Energy-Saving-App wedges itself permanently on a REJECTED simulation case ####
# Discovered while running 06. The app stopped doing anything at all and started spinning on
# /ndt/acquire_lock. Mechanism, from its own source (/home/adam/Energy-Saving-App):

  energy_saving_app.cpp:472   void send_case(...)          <-- returns VOID
  energy_saving_app.cpp:530   logs 'Simulation Request NOT Accepted' on the 502 ... and drops it
  energy_saving_app.cpp:615   canSendNextSimulation = false   (before sending)
  energy_saving_app.cpp:620   send_case(...)                  (rejected, 502)
  energy_saving_app.cpp:622   sentCase = true                 <-- SET UNCONDITIONALLY
  energy_saving_app.cpp:627   if (!sentCase) { canSendNextSimulation = true; release_lock(); }
                                              ^-- the ONLY recovery branch, and it is skipped
  energy_saving_app.cpp:366   the other way back is caseID2SwitchesDpidToPowerOff.size()
                              == completeSimulations.size(), in the simulation-COMPLETED
                              handler -- which cannot fire, because the case never ran.
  energy_saving_app.cpp:881   every later cycle: 'There is switch powering on/off, skip...'

# So one 502 leaves canSendNextSimulation == false FOREVER and routing_lock UNRELEASED.
# It is not self-healing after the simulator arrives either: 3 cases are already in
# caseID2SwitchesDpidToPowerOff and 0 in completeSimulations, and no new case can be
# prepared, so the equality at :366 can never hold again. The state is poisoned.
